            <body>
                <div class="top">
                    <div class="inner">
                        <div>
                            <h1>Resend Email Connector</h1>
                            <p class="sub">Setup guide for administrators and users</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="actions">
                            <span class="badge" style="background:#5d3d55;border-color:#5d3d55;color:#fff">Odoo 19 &amp; 20</span>
                            <a class="btn solid" href="/web#action=rex_resend_connector.action_resend_settings">Open settings</a>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="layout">
                    <div class="content">
                        <div t-if="not is_admin" class="note">
                            Only administrators can change this configuration. This page can be read by every user.
                        </div>

                        <div class="status">
                            <b>Current status.</b>
                            <span t-if="config['enabled'] and config['api_key']">Resend is enabled.</span>
                            <span t-if="not config['enabled']">The master switch is off, email goes through SMTP.</span>
                            <span t-if="config['enabled'] and not config['api_key']">The master switch is on but no API key is set.</span>
                            <br/>
                            <b>Webhook URL:</b> <code t-out="webhook_url"/>
                        </div>

                        <h2 id="about">1. What the module does</h2>
                        <p>Odoo prepares email as usual: templates, quotations, invoices, chatter notifications,
                           mass mailings, attachments, Bcc and alias domains. The module replaces only the transport.
                           Instead of opening an SMTP connection, the message is sent to the Resend API over HTTPS,
                           and the events Resend reports are written back to the Odoo record.</p>
                        <p>Incoming mail can be received from Resend as well. The module downloads the original message,
                           restores the reference to the Odoo thread and passes it to Odoo's mail gateway, so replies
                           appear in the chatter.</p>

                        <h2 id="before">2. Before you start</h2>
                        <ul>
                            <li>You can log in to Odoo as an administrator.</li>
                            <li>You have access to the DNS records of the sending domain.</li>
                            <li>Odoo has a public HTTPS address. It is required for delivery webhooks.</li>
                            <li>You have a Resend account (a free plan is enough for testing).</li>
                        </ul>

                        <h2 id="key">3. Create a Resend account and API key</h2>
                        <ol>
                            <li>Create an account on <a href="https://resend.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">resend.com</a>.</li>
                            <li>Open API Keys and create a key. Full access is needed to manage domains and webhooks
                                from Odoo. Sending access is enough if the domain and the webhook are configured in
                                the Resend dashboard.</li>
                            <li>Copy the key. It starts with <code>re_</code>.</li>
                        </ol>

                        <h2 id="domain">4. Verify a sending domain</h2>
                        <ol>
                            <li>Open <b>Resend &gt; Domains</b>, create the domain and click <b>Register in Resend</b>.</li>
                            <li>Copy the SPF and DKIM records shown on the form to your DNS provider.</li>
                            <li>Add a DMARC record, for example <code>v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:dmarc@example.com</code>.</li>
                            <li>Click <b>Verify Now</b> and wait for DNS propagation.</li>
                        </ol>
                        <img src="/rex_resend_connector/static/description/img/06_domain_form.png" alt="Domain and DNS records"/>
                        <div class="caption">Each domain shows the DNS records Resend expects and its verification status.</div>
                        <p>A subdomain such as <b>mg.example.com</b> is recommended, so the reputation of the email
                           domain is independent from the main website.</p>

                        <div t-if="domains">
                            <h3>Domains on this installation</h3>
                            <table>
                                <thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
                                <tbody>
                                    <tr t-foreach="domains" t-as="domain">
                                        <td><t t-out="domain.name"/></td>
                                        <td><span class="badge" t-out="domain.status"/></td>
                                    </tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>

                        <h2 id="configure">5. Configure outgoing email</h2>
                        <ol>
                            <li>In <b>Settings &gt; Discuss &gt; Resend</b> tick <b>Send emails through Resend</b>,
                                paste the API key and set the <b>From address</b> on the verified domain.</li>
                            <li>Leave <b>Rewrite From</b> on its default value. Odoo may choose a sender on a domain
                                Resend does not know; the module then sends from the verified address and keeps the
                                original sender in Reply-To.</li>
                            <li>Open <b>Settings &gt; Technical &gt; Outgoing Mail Servers</b>, tick
                                <b>Use Resend API</b> on the server Odoo should use and click <b>Test connection</b>.</li>
                        </ol>
                        <img src="/rex_resend_connector/static/description/img/03_settings.png" alt="Resend settings"/>
                        <div class="caption">Settings &gt; Discuss &gt; Resend</div>
                        <p>Servers without the option keep using SMTP. The master switch disables Resend for all
                           servers at once.</p>

                        <h2 id="test">6. Send a test email</h2>
                        <p>Open a quotation or an invoice and send it by email, then open <b>Resend &gt; Emails</b>.
                           The row shows the Resend id and the status. The test email button in the settings sends a
                           message through the full pipeline.</p>
                        <p>Without a verified domain, Resend accepts only these recipients:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li><code>delivered@resend.dev</code>: delivered;</li>
                            <li><code>bounced@resend.dev</code>: hard bounce;</li>
                            <li><code>complained@resend.dev</code>: delivered, then marked as spam;</li>
                            <li><code>suppressed@resend.dev</code>: suppressed address.</li>
                        </ul>

                        <h2 id="webhook">7. Delivery webhooks</h2>
                        <ol>
                            <li>Check the <b>Webhook URL</b> in the settings. Odoo must be reachable from the internet
                                at that address. If needed, set <b>Public Base URL</b> to the public address.</li>
                            <li>Click <b>Create / update webhook in Resend</b>. The endpoint is created, subscribed to
                                the email events and the signing secret is stored.</li>
                            <li>Open <b>Resend &gt; Configuration &gt; Webhook Events</b> to see the calls received from
                                Resend.</li>
                        </ol>
                        <pre>email.sent, email.delivered, email.delivery_delayed, email.opened,
email.clicked, email.bounced, email.complained, email.failed,
email.suppressed, email.received</pre>
                        <img src="/rex_resend_connector/static/description/img/08_webhook_events.png" alt="Webhook events"/>
                        <div class="caption">Every webhook call is listed with its type, status and payload.</div>
                        <p>Each call is verified with the Svix HMAC-SHA256 signature, a five minute tolerance and a
                           unique event id. Calls that cannot be processed immediately are retried by a scheduled job.</p>

                        <h2 id="inbound">8. Receive incoming email</h2>
                        <ol>
                            <li>Add the MX record of a subdomain, for example <b>reply.example.com</b>, to your DNS provider.
                                Resend uses the record with the lowest priority.</li>
                            <li>Set <b>Settings &gt; Discuss &gt; Alias Domain</b> to that subdomain.</li>
                            <li>Create a mail alias for the address, for example <b>sales@reply.example.com</b>, or simply
                                reply to an email sent from Odoo.</li>
                        </ol>
                        <img src="/rex_resend_connector/static/description/img/07_inbound_list.png" alt="Inbound emails"/>
                        <div class="caption">Messages without a matching alias are kept with the No Route status.</div>
                        <p>Every address on the receiving domain is accepted by Resend. Routing is done by Odoo.</p>

                        <h2 id="status">9. Delivery statuses</h2>
                        <img src="/rex_resend_connector/static/description/img/02_email_form.png" alt="Delivery history"/>
                        <div class="caption">Each email keeps its event history and the Resend identifiers.</div>
                        <table>
                            <thead><tr><th>Status</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Odoo</th></tr></thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr><td>Sent</td><td>Accepted by the Resend API</td><td>Email sent</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>Delivered</td><td>Accepted by the recipient server</td><td>Notification delivered</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>Delivery delayed</td><td>Resend is still retrying</td><td>Warning only</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>Opened / Clicked</td><td>Tracking events</td><td>Informational</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>Bounced</td><td>Rejected by the recipient server</td><td>Email failed, notification bounced</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>Complained</td><td>Marked as spam by the recipient</td><td>Notification cancelled</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>Failed</td><td>Quota, invalid data, blocked attachment</td><td>Email failed with the reason</td></tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>

                        <h2 id="troubleshooting">10. Troubleshooting</h2>
                        <details>
                            <summary>The email is not sent</summary>
                            <p>Open the email and read the failure reason. It contains the Resend error, for example
                               domain is not verified, invalid_api_key or daily_quota_exceeded.</p>
                        </details>
                        <details>
                            <summary>No delivery status appears</summary>
                            <p>Open Resend &gt; Configuration &gt; Webhook Events. If the list is empty, the webhook is
                               missing or Odoo is not reachable from the internet.</p>
                        </details>
                        <details>
                            <summary>The webhook answers 401</summary>
                            <p>The signing secret does not match. Copy the secret from the Resend dashboard again and
                               check the server clock.</p>
                        </details>
                        <details>
                            <summary>Replies do not appear in the chatter</summary>
                            <p>Check the MX record, the email.received subscription, the alias domain and the Inbound
                               list for messages without a route.</p>
                        </details>
                        <details>
                            <summary>Mass mailing is slow</summary>
                            <p>Resend allows 10 requests per second per team. The module limits itself to 8 and retries
                               the rest, so the mailing takes longer but no message is lost.</p>
                        </details>

                        <h2 id="security">11. Security</h2>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Webhook calls are verified with the Svix signature, a constant time comparison and a
                                five minute tolerance. Duplicate calls are ignored.</li>
                            <li>The API key and the signing secret are system parameters that only administrators can read.
                                They are never written to the log.</li>
                            <li>Each email is sent with an idempotency key, so a retry cannot deliver it twice.</li>
                            <li>Attachments are checked against the file types and the size allowed by Resend before sending.</li>
                        </ul>

